# CCAR-F Retake Drill — Weak Objectives Only


**Design rules applied to every question**, per your instructions:
- All four options are genuine, defensible architectural moves — none is a throwaway or obviously
  wrong distractor. Difficulty comes from precision, not elimination.
- Options are matched in length and tone so the correct answer isn't identifiable by looking
  longer, more hedged, or more "complete" than the others.
- The correct answer is stated concisely — the same register as the distractors, not a giveaway.
- Full rationale (why the right one is right, and precisely why each distractor falls short) is
  in the **Answer Key** at the bottom only — not inline, so you can self-test cold.

Work through a section, then check the key. Domain tags reflect the CCAR-F blueprint domain each
